    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0156" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg88"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1984.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 17, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit a letter of the 13th instant
                    from James Rogers, of No. 8 Wall street, New York, and the original depositions
                    which accompanied it, relative to the case of William Jackson, otherwise called
                    John McCafferty, reported to be under sentence of death for high treason in
                    Ireland.</p>
                <p>You will make the most effective use of them you can, in using your good offices
                    on behalf of the prisoner to obtain his release or a mitigation of his
                    sentence.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
